# Copy to `.env.local` and adjust. Committed as documentation — never put secrets here.
#
# The aylayoo-service REST API. Inlined into the client bundle at build time, so it must be
# set when you build, and setting it only at runtime does nothing for browser code.
#
# Local development (the Worker's dev port):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4003
#
# Production (set this in the Vercel project's Environment Variables):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://aylayoo-service.sbolorsaikhan4.workers.dev
#
# The API only answers browsers from an origin in its own allow-list
# (aylayoo-service/wrangler.jsonc → vars.ALLOWED_ORIGINS): http://localhost:3000,
# http://localhost:5173 and https://ayalyoo-web.vercel.app. That is why `nx dev` pins port
# 3000 — on any other port the browser blocks every request as a CORS failure.
